<title>ITALY: Italy has global trade surplus in Jan.</title>
<headline>Italy has global trade surplus in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy had a 3.247 trln lire global</p>
<p>trade surplus in January, the Italian Exchange Office said in a</p>
<p>statement.</p>
<p> ITALIAN TRADE BALANCE	Jan 97	  Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p> Amount (lire)	     +3.247 trln   +3.591 trln   +2.109</p>
<p> Cumulative yr to date   +3.247 trln  +41.929 trln   +2.109</p>
<p>Note: The calculation is based on flows through the financial sector on transactions in excess of 20 million lire.</p>
</text>
